module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Pretopology
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-! # Continuous functors between sites

## Main results

* `StacksContinuousFunctor.IsContinuous`: a functor between sites given by pretopologies is
  *continuous* when it takes coverings to coverings and preserves the fibre products
  occurring in a covering (Stacks 00WV).

The faithful notion of Stacks 00WV, for sites given by indexed covering families, is
`Stacks.Sites.Site.IsContinuous`, which carries the tag.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace StacksContinuousFunctor

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] [HasPullbacks C]
variable {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] [HasPullbacks D]

/-- **Stacks 00WV.** A functor `u : C ⥤ D` between sites given by pretopologies `J` and `K`
is *continuous* if for every covering `S` of an object `V` in `J` the family obtained by
pushing `S` forward covers `u V`, and `u` turns the fibre products of a covering arrow with
an arbitrary arrow into fibre products in `D`.

**Warning: `cover_pushforward` below is NOT clause (1) of Tag 00WV, and this structure is
strictly stronger than the source's notion.**  Tag 00WV asks that the *image family*
`{u Vᵢ → u V}_{i ∈ I}`, with the same index set, be a covering.  `Presieve.functorPushforward`
is instead the sieve *generated by* that family, so it also contains every arrow factoring
through a member of it.  Coverings of a `Pretopology` are not required to be downward closed,
so the two conditions are incomparable in general — see the discussion in
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Hypercovering.Basic`, which states the faithful clause as
`MapsCoveringsToCoverings`.

How much stronger: Stacks' Definition 00WV is satisfied by the identity functor of *every*
site, trivially.  This structure is not — `𝟭` of the two-element lattice site under the
trivial pretopology fails `cover_pushforward`, because the downward closure of `{𝟙 ⊤}` also
contains `⊥ ⟶ ⊤` and so is not the singleton presieve.  That is a machine-checked
counterexample, not a suspicion.  So what is formalized here implies Tag 00WV's clause (2)
faithfully (`pullback_iso`) but replaces its clause (1) by a condition the source's own examples
do not satisfy.

The structure is kept because around ninety files in this tree construct it, and
`MapsCoveringsToCoverings` carries the faithful clause (1) for the consumers that need it; the
Stacks tag 00WV is carried by `Stacks.Sites.Site.IsContinuous`, the source's notion.  Anything
relying on this structure *as* Tag 00WV should be read against this warning first. -/
structure IsContinuous (u : C ⥤ D) (J : Pretopology C) (K : Pretopology D) :
    Prop where
  /-- The pushforward of a `J`-covering of `V` is a `K`-covering of `u V`. -/
  cover_pushforward :
    ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ ⦃S : Presieve V⦄, S ∈ J.coverings V →
      S.functorPushforward u ∈ K.coverings (u.obj V)
  /-- For a covering arrow `f : Y ⟶ V` and an arbitrary `g : T ⟶ V`, the canonical map
  `u (T ×_V Y) ⟶ u T ×_{u V} u Y` is an isomorphism. -/
  pullback_iso :
    ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ ⦃S : Presieve V⦄, S ∈ J.coverings V →
      ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ ⦃f : Y ⟶ V⦄, S f → ∀ ⦃T : C⦄ (g : T ⟶ V),
        IsIso (pullbackComparison u g f)

end StacksContinuousFunctor
